============================================================

Ontologies




------


To find following ontologies in MOBI: Login to Mobi. Open Catalog -> Search and type the ontology title, or search REO to see all REO-tagged ontologies.


Basic Formal Ontology (BFO)

Summary: Upper ontology that provides the common, domain-neutral backbone for all REO ontologies (continuants vs. occurrents, parthood, qualities, roles).
Coverage (key classes): Continuant, Independent Continuant, Material Entity, Object, Quality, Role, Disposition, Process, Process Boundary.
Relations: part_of / has_part, participates_in, has_quality, has_role, bearer_of, realized_in, preceded_by.
Alignments: ISO/IEC 21838-2; foundation for REO, CCO, IOF-Core.

RTX Enterprise Ontology (REO) — Mid-Level

Summary: Mid-level ontology (BFO-based) that standardizes enterprise-wide patterns (agents, artifacts, information, time, units, events) for cross-BU interoperability.
Coverage: Agent, Organization, Artifact, Information Entity, Measurement, Unit, Time Instant/Interval, Event, Location, Facility.
Relations: about, created_by, used_in, located_in, measured_by, has_unit, has_temporal_extent, generates, consumes.
Alignments: Extends BFO; draws patterns from CCO and IOF.

REO Aircraft Engine Diagnostic, Prognostic & Health Management (DPHM) Ontology

Summary: Semantics for engine health: signals, conditions, faults, diagnostics, prognostics, and maintenance recommendations.
Coverage: Engine, Subsystem, Sensor, Signal, Health Indicator, Fault, Diagnostic Result, Prognostic Forecast, Remaining Useful Life, Alert.
Relations: observes / observed_on, indicates, derived_from, triggers, mitigated_by, applies_to, depends_on.
Alignments: REO (mid-level), CCO (Artifact/Function), IOF-Maintenance.

REO Supply Chain Ontology

Summary: End-to-end supply semantics for parts, BoMs, suppliers, orders, shipments, and inventory across programs.
Coverage: Part, Part Version, BoM Item, Supplier, Purchase Order, Sales Order, Shipment, Inventory, Lot/Batch, Contract.
Relations: has_component, sourced_from, fulfills, ships_to, allocated_to, substitutes_for, governed_by.
Alignments: REO; CCO (Artifact, Organization), IOF-Core (Process/Resource).

REO Maintenance, Repair & Overhaul (MRO) Ontology

Summary: Common language for maintenance planning and execution: tasks, workcards, resources, findings, and dispositions.
Coverage: Maintenance Task, Work Order, Procedure, Tool, Skill, Finding, Nonconformance, Disposition, Downtime, Turn-Around-Time.
Relations: requires_tool, requires_skill, results_in, disposition_of, scheduled_for, performed_by, applies_to_config.
Alignments: REO; IOF-Maintenance; CCO (Agent, Artifact, Process).

REO Information Artifact Ontology

Summary: Models documents and formal records—requirements, specs, drawings, test reports, datasets—with provenance and status.
Coverage: Information Artifact, Requirement, Specification, Drawing, Test Report, Dataset, Revision, Approval, Signature.
Relations: about, conforms_to, version_of, approved_by, supersedes, cites, derived_from.
Alignments: REO; based on CCO/IAO-style patterns.

REO Units of Measure Ontology

Summary: Enterprise units, quantities, and conversions to make measurements interoperable and computable.
Coverage: Unit, Quantity Kind, Measurement, Value, Conversion, Tolerance, Precision.
Relations: has_unit, has_quantity_kind, has_value, convertible_to, within_tolerance_of.
Alignments: REO; maps to QUDT/UCUM concepts as needed.

REO Time Ontology

Summary: Shared model of instants, intervals, calendars, and recurrence for temporal reasoning across data sets.
Coverage: Time Instant, Time Interval, Duration, Recurrence, Timeline, Temporal Relation.
Relations: starts_at, ends_at, overlaps, during, before, after, equals.
Alignments: REO; compatible with OWL-Time patterns.

REO Quality Ontology

Summary: Represents measurable/qualitative characteristics of artifacts and processes (e.g., temperature, surface roughness, defect severity).
Coverage: Quality, Characteristic, Threshold, Spec Limit, Conformance State, Nonconformance Severity.
Relations: has_quality, has_spec_limit, violates, within_spec, measured_by.
Alignments: REO; BFO (Quality), IOF-Core.

REO Aircraft Engine Digital Twin Ontology

Summary: Canonical model of engine configurations, states, telemetry, inspections, and lifecycle events for digital-twin analytics.
Coverage: Engine, Configuration, Serial Numbered Item, Assembly, Inspection, Measurement, State, Event, Simulation Run.
Relations: has_configuration, configuration_of, inspected_by, generates_signal, simulated_as, affected_by_event.
Alignments: REO; CCO (Artifact), IOF-Core/Maintenance.

REO Event Ontology

Summary: Uniform representation of business and technical events (observations, changes, transactions) with time and provenance.
Coverage: Event, Observation, Change, Transaction, Cause, Effect, Context.
Relations: occurs_at, about, has_cause, has_effect, reported_by, recorded_in.
Alignments: REO; BFO (Process/Process Boundary); compatible with event-sourcing patterns.

REO Agent Ontology

Summary: People, organizations, roles, competencies, and responsibilities used across programs and factories.
Coverage: Person, Organization, Team, Role, Credential, Competency, Responsibility, Contact Point.
Relations: plays_role, member_of, responsible_for, reports_to, qualified_for.
Alignments: REO; CCO (Agent, Organization).

REO Artifact Ontology

Summary: Physical artifacts and their design/realization views, including configurations and identification.
Coverage: Artifact, Design, Part, Assembly, Serial Item, Material, Feature, Version, Configuration Item.
Relations: realizes_design, has_part, identified_by, made_of, configured_as, substitutes_for.
Alignments: REO; CCO (Artifact, Design); ties into Supply Chain & Digital Twin ontologies.

REO Maintenance Ontology

Summary: Lightweight core for maintenance concepts (when MRO depth isn’t required) focused on tasks, intervals, and compliance.
Coverage: Maintenance Task, Interval, Compliance, Threshold, Alert, Work Package.
Relations: due_at, due_by, satisfied_by, escalates_to, grouped_in.
Alignments: REO; IOF-Maintenance.

REO Facility Ontology

Summary: Standardizes sites, buildings, cells, lines, stations, and equipment for manufacturing and test.
Coverage: Site, Building, Area, Cell, Line, Station, Equipment, Capability, Shift.
Relations: located_in, contains, uses_equipment, has_capability, operates_during.
Alignments: REO; CCO (Facility/Artifact); integrates with Geospatial & Agent.

REO Geospatial Ontology

Summary: Locations, regions, coordinate systems, and geometry references for mapping assets, events, and routes.
Coverage: Geo Feature, Point, Line, Polygon, CRS, Address, Route, Region.
Relations: has_geometry, within, intersects, along_route, near, encoded_in_crs.
Alignments: REO; compatible with GeoSPARQL patterns.

REO Information Entity Ontology

Summary: Profile for datasets, API payloads, messages, logs, and records with lineage and schema annotations.
Coverage: Information Entity, Dataset, Table, Field, API Message, Schema, Lineage Step, Transformation.
Relations: describes, has_field, conforms_to_schema, produced_by, consumed_by, lineage_of.
Alignments: REO; CCO/IAO-style; complements Information Artifact Ontology (documents/records).


=========================================


Permanent vs. Temporary Components (Temporal Parthood)

Short description: Distinguish essential-for-lifetime parts from replaceable parts using bfo:hasContinuantPartAtAllTimes (permanent) vs bfo:hasContinuantPartAtSomeTime (temporary). Enables identity-safe BoMs and maintenance reasoning (e.g., current vs. original parts).



Assembly & Components (IOF/BFO BoM Backbone)

Short description: Model an assembly and its components as material entities connected by appropriate parthood relations— a minimal, stable backbone for Bills of Material before layering roles, qualities, or time.



Assembly with Component Qualities (CCO-style Extension)

Short description: Attach measurable characteristics (e.g., thickness, length) as qualities that inhere_in components, with values and units. Cleanly separates structure (part-whole) from metrics for specs/tolerance checks.



Agents, Roles & Organizations with Rigorous Naming

Short description: Represent people/organizations via roles and capture names/IDs as information content entities stored on information-bearing entities (with text values and provenance), rather than raw strings on the agent.



Information About an Entity (About-ness)

Short description: Link information to things with precise “about-ness” relations: designates (unique ID), denotes (class/type), describes (qualitative info), prescribes (rules/specs). Clarifies identifiers vs. names vs. descriptions vs. requirements.


Modeling Physical Objects: Assembly & Components (IOF/ BFO)

Short description: Minimal BoM backbone: model the assembly and each component as bfo:MaterialEntity and relate them with bfo:hasContinuantPartAtSomeTime (parts may be installed/replaced over the asset’s life). Optionally extend with CCO-style qualities—e.g., thickness, length—as specifically dependent continuants that inheres_in each component, with value and unit, when you need measurable attributes.



Agent as an Engineered System

Short description: Treat automated systems (software/hardware) as agents that can play business roles and participate in processes (e.g., an inventory system acting as a buyer and placing purchase orders), not just humans or orgs.
